 ## What would and would not help

 - ABI-specific delivery is the only meaningful remaining lever. Removing the three non-arm64 ABIs saves at most 2,115,467 compressed bytes. Releases intentionally ship one universal APK, so this would mean publishing and testing per-ABI artifacts.
-- Removing QuickJS or Sentry is not supported. Their native sizes are upper bounds, not real savings once the features are gone.
+- The measurements above predate the QuickJS-free InnerTubeX integration. QuackJS uses Kotlin player programs and removes the cipher native runtime; remeasure a fresh APK before claiming savings. Sentry remains supported and bundled in release.
 - Deleting translations or images to chase size is not warranted.
 - Installed footprint is not APK size. A device extracts only its own ABI's natives (about 1.76 MB raw on arm64 with legacy packaging), and ART data, caches and downloads vary.

diff --git a/docs/innertube.md b/docs/innertube.md
index 55b5a6c5f773859867fe43dbe2b7a9654b1830e3..59c441966b3a8a57db766df736c8fa84e44eb802 100644
--- a/docs/innertube.md
+++ b/docs/innertube.md
@@ -2,6 +2,18 @@

 InnerTubeX, the YouTube streaming engine, lives in its own repository and is pinned with `innerTubeXVersion` in `gradle.properties`. This page covers how Metrolist uses it and how to test it against live YouTube.

+## Local QuickJS-free integration
+
+Use an InnerTubeX publication migrated to QuackJS, not the unchanged remote release. No app version or remote dependency pin is changed by this companion patch.
+
+1. In QuackJS, run `./gradlew jvmTest testAndroidHostTest assemble publishToMavenLocal`.
+2. In the privately migrated InnerTubeX snapshot, run `./gradlew -PuseMavenLocalQuackJS -PGROUP=com.github.MetrolistGroup.innertubex -PVERSION_NAME=v0.10.0-quackjs-SNAPSHOT desktopTest testAndroidHostTest apiCheck assemble publishToMavenLocal`.
+3. In Metrolist, use `./gradlew -PuseMavenLocalInnerTubeX -PinnerTubeXVersion=v0.10.0-quackjs-SNAPSHOT :shared:desktopTest :shared:testAndroidHostTest :androidApp:assembleDebug :desktopApp:assemble`. This uses the existing Maven Local opt-in and actual locally published InnerTubeX coordinates, with QuackJS resolved transitively. Do not combine this with `-PuseLocalInnerTubeX`.
+
+`prewarmEjs` and the preprocessed-player-cache APIs are compatibility no-ops; persisted EJS data is ignored. Player preloads now compile Kotlin programs. Faraday supplies optional landmarks and unknown players use hint-free discovery. Unsupported player constructs return the existing extraction failure/null result, never a QuickJS fallback or unresolved signed URL. QuackJS currently handles the four verified dispatcher-style players, not arbitrary JavaScript or future player rotations.
+
+Desktop packaging no longer strips, permits or keeps QuickJS natives/classes. The APK size measurements in [android-apk-size.md](android-apk-size.md) are historical and must be rerun for this dependency graph. Live tests below remain opt-in; local fixture/build checks do not establish live playback compatibility.
+
 ## Client catalog

 The retained SABR catalog has six end-to-end validated automatic fallbacks: `ANDROID_VR_SABR`, `WEB_REMIX_SABR`, `WEB_SABR`, `TVHTML5_SIMPLY_SABR`, `MWEB_SABR` and `WEB_SAFARI_SABR`.
